---
import Base from '../../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { lessons } from '../../../../lib/object-storage/lessons.mjs';
---
<Base title="Object-storage sandbox" description="Explore object requests, conditional writes, multipart uploads and version recovery with guided local lessons inspired by Amazon S3.">
 <article class="object-sandbox">
  <header><p class="eyebrow">Playgrounds / Object storage</p><h1>Object-storage sandbox</h1><p>Change a request, predict its result and inspect what remains in the bucket.</p>
   <p class="scope">This is a local teaching model of selected S3 ideas, not Amazon S3 or an S3 emulator. It makes no network requests and needs no credentials. Your work stays in this tab’s memory and disappears on reload.</p>
  </header>
  <noscript><p>JavaScript is needed to run the model. The <a href="/learn/databases/object-storage/">articles</a> explain the ideas without it, and the <a href="/learn/databases/object-storage/practice/">real-S3 worksheet</a> provides terminal practice.</p></noscript>
  <div class="lesson-bar"><label for="lesson">Choose a lesson</label><select id="lesson"><option value="free">Explore freely</option>{Array.from(new Set(lessons.map(l=>l.group))).map(group=><optgroup label={group}>{lessons.filter(l=>l.group===group).map(l=><option value={l.id}>{l.title}</option>)}</optgroup>)}</select><button id="reset" type="button">Restart lesson</button></div>
  <p class="scope">Choosing another lesson replaces this practice state with that lesson’s starting point.</p><p id="notice" role="status"></p>
  <div id="lesson-heading"><h2 id="lesson-title"></h2><p id="lesson-description"></p><p class="scope" id="lesson-scope"></p><a id="article-link">Read the explanation →</a></div>
  <section id="starting-data" hidden aria-labelledby="starting-data-title"><h2 id="starting-data-title">The four records</h2><p>These invented coordinates stay fixed. The query and category filter are yours to change. Distance is the sum of the two squared coordinate differences.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Passage</th><th>Vector</th><th>Category</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>A</td><td>[1, 0]</td><td>billing</td></tr><tr><td>B</td><td>[0.8, 0.2]</td><td>storage</td></tr><tr><td>C</td><td>[0, 1]</td><td>storage</td></tr><tr><td>D</td><td>[-1, 0]</td><td>billing</td></tr></tbody></table></section>
  <div class="workbench">
   <section class="request-panel" aria-labelledby="request-heading"><div class="step-heading"><span id="progress"></span><h2 id="request-heading">Request</h2></div><p id="question"></p>
    <label for="request">Editable model request · JSON</label><textarea id="request" spellcheck="false" rows="10" aria-describedby="request-help"></textarea><p id="request-help" class="scope">Run one request at a time. These are playground commands, not AWS CLI syntax. Saved replies use references such as <code>$base.etag</code>.</p>
    <div class="actions"><button id="run" type="button">Run request</button><button id="next" type="button">Next step →</button><button id="restore-request" type="button">Restore this request</button></div>
    <p class="scope">Running again uses the current state. Restore changes only the editor; Restart restores the whole lesson.</p>
    <section class="response-panel" aria-labelledby="response-heading"><h2 id="response-heading">Response</h2><p id="response-status" role="status">Run the request to see its response.</p><div id="response-summary" hidden></div><details id="raw-response" open><summary>Raw model response</summary><pre id="response" tabindex="0" aria-label="Model response" hidden></pre></details><div id="explanation" hidden><h3>What to notice</h3><p id="explanation-text"></p></div></section>
   </section>
   <section class="state-panel" aria-labelledby="state-heading"><h2 id="state-heading">Bucket and application state</h2><p id="state-summary" class="scope"></p><p class="scope">This inspector shows the model’s internal state, including changes a caller with a lost reply could not yet know.</p><div id="objects"></div><details id="extra-state"><summary>Unfinished uploads and application state</summary><pre id="state-data" tabindex="0" aria-label="Uploads and application state"></pre></details><details><summary>Saved successful replies</summary><pre id="variables" tabindex="0" aria-label="Saved replies"></pre></details></section>
  </div>
  <details class="reference"><summary>Request reference and model boundaries</summary><p>All lessons use one versioning-enabled bucket. Every PUT retains a version; DELETE adds a marker. ETags are content-derived SHA-256 values prefixed with <code>model-</code>, not real S3 ETags. Requests execute sequentially. Unsupported fields are rejected.</p>
   <table><thead><tr><th>Operation</th><th>Fields after op</th><th>Result to inspect</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td>PUT</td><td>key, body; optional metadata, ifMatch or ifNoneMatch: "*"</td><td>A version, or a rejected precondition</td></tr>
    <tr><td>GET / LIST</td><td>GET: key, optional version. LIST: optional prefix</td><td>Body and identity / current names</td></tr>
    <tr><td>DELETE / DELETE_VERSION</td><td>key / key and version</td><td>A marker / removal of one version</td></tr>
    <tr><td>CREATE_UPLOAD</td><td>key</td><td>An upload ID</td></tr>
    <tr><td>UPLOAD_PART</td><td>upload, part, body</td><td>Part ETag</td></tr>
    <tr><td>COMPLETE_UPLOAD</td><td>upload, parts: [&#123;part, etag&#125;]; optional write condition</td><td>Selected parts become one object</td></tr>
    <tr><td>ABORT_UPLOAD</td><td>upload</td><td>Unfinished work disappears</td></tr>
    <tr><td>CACHE_GET / TICK</td><td>key, optional ttl / seconds</td><td>Cached copy / model time</td></tr>
    <tr><td>APP_CREATE</td><td>id, key</td><td>A pending application record</td></tr>
    <tr><td>APP_VALIDATE / APP_PUBLISH / APP_ABANDON</td><td>id</td><td>Exact-version verification / ready / abandoned</td></tr>
    <tr><td>PROCESS_EVENT</td><td>key, sequence, body; optional stopAfterOutput</td><td>Output, completion ledger and latest pointer</td></tr>
    <tr><td>COST</td><td>records, bytesPerRecord, recordsPerObject, scans; optional copies, retryFraction, rates</td><td>Full-scan request and byte arithmetic</td></tr>
    <tr><td>VECTOR_QUERY</td><td>query: [x,y]; optional topK, category</td><td>Exact distances for four invented records</td></tr>
   </tbody></table>
   <p><code>saveAs</code> saves a successful reply, such as <code>"saveAs":"base"</code>. Later fields can use <code>"$base.etag"</code> or <code>"$base.version"</code>. <code>loseReply:true</code> applies a successful operation but withholds its reply; the caller must reconcile. It does not save a response variable.</p>
   <p>The model omits IAM, signatures, CORS, network timing, real multipart sizes, checksums, listing pagination, Object Lock, lifecycle scheduling, replication and AWS pricing. Application, cache, cost and vector operations are explicitly local models. It limits text bodies, key counts and history to keep this tab responsive. Use <a href="/learn/databases/object-storage/practice/">the real-S3 worksheet</a> to test actual service responses.</p>
  </details>
  <details class="history"><summary>Requests run in this lesson</summary><ol id="history"></ol></details>
  <nav class="onward"><a href="/learn/databases/object-storage/">Object-storage collection →</a><a href="/playgrounds/">All playgrounds →</a><a href="/learn/databases/object-storage/practice/">Try real S3 →</a></nav>
 </article>
</Base>
<script>
 import '../../../../lib/object-storage/sandbox';
</script>
<style>
 :global(body:has(.object-sandbox) main) { max-width:76rem; }
 #response { white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere; }
 #starting-data { max-width:46rem; margin:1.5rem 0 2rem; }
 #starting-data table { width:100%;display:table; }
 .object-sandbox { max-width:76rem; margin:auto; font-family:var(--font-sans); min-width:0; }
 header { max-width:53rem; } h1 { font-size:clamp(2.2rem,5vw,3.8rem); } p { line-height:1.7; }
 .scope { font-size:.86rem; color:var(--color-text-secondary); }.scope code { overflow-wrap:anywhere; }
 button,select,textarea { font:inherit; color:var(--color-text); background:var(--color-surface); border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); border-radius:5px; }
 button,select { min-height:44px; padding:.6rem .8rem; } button { cursor:pointer; } button:disabled { opacity:.5;cursor:default; }
 button:hover:not(:disabled) { border-color:var(--color-accent); } :is(button,select,textarea,summary,a,pre):focus-visible { outline:3px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:3px; }
 .lesson-bar { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:.7rem; border-block:1px solid var(--color-rule);padding:1rem 0;margin:2rem 0 1rem; } select { max-width:100%;flex:1;min-width:0; }
 #lesson-heading { max-width:52rem;margin:1.5rem 0 2rem; } #lesson-heading h2 { margin-bottom:.6rem; }
 .workbench { display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.2fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:2rem;align-items:start; }
 .request-panel,.state-panel { min-width:0; }.request-panel { border-top:3px solid var(--color-accent);padding-top:1rem; }.state-panel { background:var(--color-surface-alt);padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule); }
 h2 { font-size:1.35rem;margin-top:0; } h3 { font-size:1rem; } #progress { font-size:.8rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary); } label { display:block;font-size:.85rem;margin-bottom:.5rem; }
 textarea { width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;resize:vertical;padding:1rem;font:.85rem/1.65 var(--font-mono);min-height:13rem;tab-size:2; }
 .actions { display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.7rem; } #run { background:var(--color-accent);color:var(--color-surface);border-color:var(--color-accent); } .response-panel { margin-top:2rem;border-top:1px solid var(--color-rule);padding-top:1rem; }
 pre { max-width:100%;font-size:.78rem;line-height:1.65;overflow:auto;max-height:28rem; } #explanation { border-left:2px solid var(--color-accent);padding-left:1rem; } #explanation h3 {margin-bottom:.3rem;}
 details { margin:1rem 0; } summary {cursor:pointer;line-height:1.7;} .reference,.history {border-top:1px solid var(--color-rule);padding:1rem 0;} table {display:block;overflow:auto;font-size:.85rem;}th,td {padding:.6rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule);}
 .onward {display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1rem 2rem;border-top:1px solid var(--color-rule);padding:1.4rem 0;}
 #notice:empty {display:none;} #notice {border-left:2px solid var(--color-accent);padding-left:1rem;}
 :global(.object-item) {border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule);padding:.6rem 0;} :global(.object-item summary) {overflow-wrap:anywhere;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.8rem;}
 :global(.object-item .object-body) {white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;margin:.6rem 0;font-size:.8rem;}
 :global(#history li) {overflow-wrap:anywhere;margin-bottom:1rem;font-size:.85rem;}
 @media(max-width:850px){.workbench{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}.state-panel{padding:1rem}.lesson-bar label{width:100%} .lesson-bar select{flex-basis:65%} }
</style>
